# Example CODEOWNERS for a repo that uses slsec. Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS (GitHub) or the
# equivalent for your Git server, replace @your-org/appsec, and require code-owner review on the
# default branch. These files decide what CI enforces; the setup gate checks some of them
# (docs/security-overview.md#what-the-gate-doesnt-check).

# CI definitions
/.github/workflows/       @your-org/appsec
/Jenkinsfile              @your-org/appsec

# slsec and pre-commit configuration
/.pre-commit-config.yaml  @your-org/appsec
/.slsec.yaml              @your-org/appsec

# Tool configs and suppression files
/.gitleaks.toml           @your-org/appsec
/.gitleaksignore          @your-org/appsec
/.hadolint.yaml           @your-org/appsec
/.tflint.hcl              @your-org/appsec
/zizmor.yml               @your-org/appsec
/.groovylintrc.json       @your-org/appsec

# Dependency update policy
/renovate.json            @your-org/appsec
